# uhub — outstanding work

State: master is 0.9.0-dev (CMakeLists.txt, build.zig, build.zig.zon; see
doc/release.txt for the pre-release label). 0.8.1 (0.8.0 plus the #127 - #130
security fixes) was released from the 0.8.x-stable branch.

## HBRI
- A failed or lost ITCP challenge is not retried within a session; the client
  must reconnect. Deliberate — one outstanding challenge per session bounds the
  ITCP-per-INF-update amplification — but revisit if it proves too strict.
- HBRI e2e now exists (test/e2e/run_hbri_e2e.sh, wired into the CI coverage
  job), covering TLS and stale validations (including onto a recycled SID).
- The HBRI token MAC now binds connection_id rather than tm_connected, closing
  the same-second SID takeover the seconds-granular timestamp allowed. Covered
  at both levels (autotest/test_hbri.tcc, run_hbri_e2e.sh phase 8).

## Retiring plain text
Goal: every network connection uhub makes or accepts is TLS. Unix-domain
sockets (worker links) are host-local and stay unwrapped.

Done:
- Hub links: a hub with tls_enable dials its TCP peers over TLS and refuses
  plain-text links (doc/linking.txt).

Phase 1 -- TLS by default, plain text only on request:
- tls_require defaults to on. Warn at startup when tls_enable or tls_require
  is off.
- Metrics: plain HTTP only from localhost; anything else over HTTPS with the
  hub's certificate. http_redirect_addr redirects to https://.
- reg_server_url refuses http://; the hub advertises only adcs:// addresses
  (regserver.c, hub.c).
- !redirect accepts only adcs:// (adc:// goes, and dchub:// is NMDC).

Phase 2 -- hub links fully authenticated:
- Per-node keys pinned inside TLS (WireGuard-style: each node holds its own
  private key and its peers' public keys). Replaces the shared link_secret
  over TCP, and with it the handshake relay that TLS without channel binding
  still allows. Open: which certificate the accepting side presents, since
  links share the client port; LibreSSL Ed25519 support at our floor.
- Remove the plain-TCP link path.

Phase 3 -- remove the off switches:
- Retire tls_enable and tls_require; the probe refuses plain ADC and plain
  HTTP (metrics on localhost excepted). Open: answer a plain ADC client with a
  one-line redirect to adcs://, or close without a word.
- Client-to-client: stop relaying CTM/RCM that ask for plain ADC/1.0; the
  seeder and uhub-fuse refuse plain transfers. Most likely to break real
  clients -- consider shipping it as an option first.
- Tools (adcclient, adcrush, linktest, uhub-seeder, uhub-fuse) drop adc://.
- Integration tests move to TLS; unit tests of internal APIs may keep plain
  socketpairs.
- Docs and packaging: doc/uhub.conf, README, uhub.spec, uhub.ebuild.

TLS versions: 1.2 is the default floor (tls_version, configurable to 1.3), and
TLS 1.3 is always offered -- openssl.c sets a minimum version only. Keep it so.

## Networking / platform
- Windows: the WINSOCK paths in src/network/network.c are done (readable
  error text, keepalive tuning, inet_ntop/inet_pton, the local address family).
  autotest still does not build for Windows -- it relies on POSIX socket
  semantics -- so test/e2e/run_windows_wine_e2e.sh (zig + wine, not in CI) is
  the runtime check; the CI windows job only starts uhub.exe.

## Cleanup
- Branch sprawl: 27 local and 34 remote branches, mostly unmerged historical
  topic branches (gnutls_work, libevent_work, visual_studio_2010_work, ...).
  Tag-then-delete historical work; delete locals that only mirror origin.

## Resolved since the 0.6.1 assessment (ASSESSMENT.md)
ASSESSMENT.md is pinned to 0.6.1 and is stale on these points:
- Version drift — CMakeLists.txt, build.zig and build.zig.zon now agree.
- Stale release tooling in admin/ — the directory is gone.
- Dockerfile in-tree build — now `cmake -S . -B build`.
- Untested connection.c state machine and TLS — autotest/test_connect.tcc and
  autotest/test_tls.tcc now exist.
- HBRI was undocumented — now covered in doc/architecture.txt and
  doc/uhub.conf.
- HBRI was unreachable at login for nat_override users — check_network() now
  records the intent before returning. Only for an IPv6 secondary: over IPv6
  the secondary family is the IPv4 address nat_override exists to trust, and
  check_hbri_update() carries the same guard.
- Stale FIXME at hub.c claiming HH/WS/NE/OW are missing — removed; they are
  implemented in the same function and in regserver.c.
- Raw ADC status codes in hub.c — already named (ADC_STATUS_*).
- "Flood control should be a plugin" — the privileged-chat half is done.
  chat_is_privileged / msg_chat_is_privileged are now obsolete options
  (warn-and-ignore, via the new "obsolete" type in config.xml) and the policy
  lives in mod_chat_is_privileged, which gained msg_mainchat / msg_privchat
  parameters. Only mute is left in core, and that is hub state, not policy.
